The hermes-safe-update binaries do not include Hermes Agent source code. They
run the user's own installed copy of Hermes (its launcher, its bundled Python
and its bundled Electron) and read files that Hermes writes. Small pieces of
text that Hermes prints (progress lines, a few error messages) are matched as
data and listed in internal/hermes/contracts.go.

The source repository also holds an example hook,
examples/hooks/bundled-skill-merge (not part of the binaries or the release
archives). It imports the user's installed Hermes code at run time. Two short
functions in it (read_manifest and set_manifest_entry) re-implement the
manifest format and read/write idiom of Hermes Agent's tools/skills_sync.py;
that idiom is MIT-licensed, Copyright (c) 2025 Nous Research.

